{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And if thus You do to me</b> — Moses' strength failed like a woman's, for the Holy One, blessed be He, had shown him the punishment that He was destined to bring upon them. Therefore he said before Him: If this is the case, kill me, I pray, by killing — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 11:15). But I do not understand this, for the form אַתְּ directed upward is the feminine form. But according to the way of peshat, the usage of the language occurs also for a masculine noun: <b>אַתְּ כְּרוּב מִמְשַׁח הַסּוֹכֵךְ</b> (Ezekiel 28:14). And by way of truth, 'if thus You do to me' — it speaks in the attribute of Judgment, as it says, <b>וַיִּחַר אַף ה' מְאֹד</b> (Numbers 11:10). And likewise, <b>וְאַתְּ תְּדַבֵּר אֵלֵינוּ</b> (Deuteronomy 5:24) — it is an appellation for the great fire, that it will speak the words of HaShem to us, and we will hear from your mouth and do them. And likewise, <b>אַתְּ כְּרוּב מִמְשַׁח</b> — it alludes to the second cherub, and the enlightened will understand:" "And the sense of <b>kill me, I pray, by killing</b> is that You should send slayers upon me with the sword, for my death is better, even by the sword of man, than my life in this suffering. And it is possible that it is like הֲמִיתֵנִי (cause me to die), and likewise, <b>וְאַנְשֵׁיהֶם יִהְיוּ הֲרוּגֵי מָוֶת, בַּחוּרֵיהֶם מֻכֵּי חֶרֶב בַּמִּלְחָמָה</b> (Jeremiah 18:21), and likewise, <b>וּפְחִי בַהֲרוּגִים הָאֵלֶּה</b> (Ezekiel 37:9)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The first objection ('I do not understand this, for the form אַתְּ directed upward is the feminine form') appears to dispute Rashi's reading that אַתְּ indicates Moses weakened like a woman. Ramban then counters that אַתְּ is also used with masculine nouns, citing Ezekiel 28:14."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:28.835957986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}